12
01:09:42,857 --> 01:09:48,857
Notorious is a 2009 American biographical drama film based on the life of Brooklyn-based
hip-hop artist Christopher "Biggie Smalls" Wallace / the Notorious B.I.G..

13
01:15:31,428 --> 01:15:37,428
The film was directed by George Tillman Jr., and written by
Reggie Rock Bythewood and Cheo Hodari Coker.

14
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:26,000
Jamal Woolard stars as Wallace, with Angela Bassett, Derek
Luke, and Anthony Mackie in supporting roles.

15
01:27:08,571 --> 01:27:14,571
The film dramatizes key events in Biggie's life: his criminal lifestyle, arrest and release from prison, his relationships with Sean Combs (who serves as executive
producer), Tupac Shakur, Lil' Kim, and Faith Evans, his involvement in the East Coast–West Coast hip hop rivalry, and his drive-by-shooting murder on March 9, 1997.

16
01:32:57,142 --> 01:33:03,142
Biggie's mother, Voletta, served as a producer for the film,
alongside his former managers Wayne Barrow and Mark Pitts.

17
01:38:45,714 --> 01:38:51,714
Notorious was released in the United States on January
16, 2009, by Fox Searchlight Pictures.

18
01:44:34,285 --> 01:44:40,285
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise mainly aimed at
Woolard's performance and grossed $44.4 million on a $20 million budget.

19
01:50:22,857 --> 01:50:28,857
The film explores themes of rap music, ghetto, murder, death, boom box.

20
01:56:11,428 --> 01:56:17,428
The tone is emotional.
